use "testing" ;

\ The shape from mutual_tco_non_tail_arm.1z with no `compile!`. Hybrid forms the group and
\ compiles the self-recursive word once each passes the call threshold.

a: ( n -- n ) [ dup 10 > [ 1 - b ] [ dup 5 > [ 1 - b ] [ ] if 100 + ] if ] ;
b: ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - a ] [ ] if ] ;
countdown: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 10 > [ 1 - countdown ] [ dup 0 > [ 1 - countdown ] [ ] if 1 + ] if ] ;

300 [ 7 a drop 3 countdown drop ] times

"a group member call in a non-tail arm" test-section
7 a 205 "the code after the inner if runs once" assert=
12 a 404 "the code after the inner if runs at every level" assert=

"a self call in a non-tail arm" test-section
3 countdown 4 "the code after the inner if runs at every level" assert=
13 countdown 11 "the tail self call and the non-tail one mix" assert=
